PATCH 534: FUN_0000_c829 and FUN_0000_c894 -- the render method for object classes 5 and 6, and the
helper it tails into, were both MISSING.

The second and third of the three absent cockpit-view methods patch 533 uncovered.  c4df dispatches
mvec = word[STRSEG : classid*2 + 0x3632], and that table sends classes 5..6 to 0xc829, which the port
did not define and did not register in the fist_icall fmap.  0xc829 is a pure thunk into 0xc894, which
was likewise absent.

asm-verified vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin:

    c829: e8 68 00     call 0xc894
    c82c: c3           ret

    c894: b4 0f        mov ah,0xf
    c896: f6 44 16 08  testb $0x8,0x16(%si)
    c89a: 74 02        je   0xc89e            ; bit clear -> keep 0xf
    c89c: b4 0e        mov ah,0xe
    c89e: f6 44 17 08  testb $0x8,0x17(%si)
    c8a2: 74 08        je   0xc8ac            ; bit clear -> draw
    c8a4: f7 06 52 04 20 00  testw $0x20,0x452
    c8aa: 74 04        je   0xc8b0            ; blink phase clear -> skip
    c8ac: e8 03 00     call 0xc8b2
    c8af: c3           ret
    c8b0: f9           stc
    c8b1: c3           ret

So c894 is the BLINKING variant of the c8b2 draw: it draws unless the object's [si+0x17] bit 3 is set
AND the frame-timer blink bit [0x452]&0x20 is clear.  AH selects the sprite kind, 0x0e when the
object's [si+0x16] bit 3 is set and 0x0f otherwise.

Both are reconstructed in the arg-less c4df context that patch 463 established for the identical
FUN_0000_c70d: si = g_fist_render_si (the object), bx = classid*2 (live from c4df), bp -> 0.  c8b2 ends
with clc (patch 463 threads that through g_fist_cf), so only the 0xc8b0 stc path needs an explicit
g_fist_cf = 1.

With 533 and 534 in, the five cockpit-view method targets are: 0xc7ca (present), 0xc5e7 (present),
0xc829 + 0xc86e (added), 0xc715 (STILL MISSING -- classid 16; it is longer, indexes
word[DGROUP:bx-0x17f3] by byte[si+0x1c], calls 0xc8c2, and on its else path appends si to a STRSEG list
at gs:[bx+0x366a] with a 0x40 bound; left on board:0014's sibling item).

